Global Static List of EDs connected to Edge Server for collaborative inference

Inputs:
    1 Snapshot of EDs (all EDs present inside coverage area at this time),
    2 Details of Edge Server (kitne models cached hain at this time)

2 Details of all models along with EDs that are in the region currently and demanding it
3 Now I need to find out EDs which are handed in the edge server
4 Now I will compare the EDs which are present in Edge Server region currently and previously with help of Global Model Caching List + Edge Server dereference (current EDs in region)
5 Now I will find out EDs which have handed off and handed in call it list hand off and hand in
6 Check handin EDs mein konse naye models hain (handin new models)
7 Similarly handoff EDs models
8 Now find how many EDS accessing a corresponding models dict of models and EDs as values
9 Now I will choose greedily which model to cache and to swap out aur uske lie bana lenge matrix
10 Matrix (1. Number of EDs, 2. Storage, 3. Marginal Utility per Model (wrt to EDs jinhe wo model chahie))
(Number of Models are still limited and in worst case we need all EDs of list for corresponding model in that case still it will tend towards nearly O(k*n) which is O(n)
11 Now based on above matrix we get list of Models in non-increasing order Model Utility X
12 Now we will have temp list on basis of 0-1 knapsack allocate storage to Models (cache and swap on this basis)
13 Now we will update the Global list of EDs in Edge Server
14 We will modify edge server ka cache based on temp list (we will use LRU strategy)

Assumption:
1: Har Edge Server ke corresponding ek static list hogi, kitni EDs edge server ke range mein hain
2: Isko initialize karenge with global snapshot
3: We will defined a parameter corresponding to each edge server 0-100 based on certain matrix which will help EDs to know which edge server to access
4: ED directly Edge Server ko query karke cached model ki list lega for taking better decisions